content.text:
Interesting: measurements show no big gap at mobile: dialogue ends y=506, choices start 512. So the earlier screenshot with gap was from an older CSS state or maybe it was 360x640 screenshot? Wait mobile-choices.png visually had 145px gap. But current measurement at 390 says gap 6px. Maybe screenshot was from before the :has fix? Or the screenshot is 360x640? The image is 390x844. Hmm, maybe the screenshot had chapter quote and line but choices animate in with delay? The choice animation delays cause items to appear sequentially; screenshot at 400ms might catch them. Not gap.

Actually wait, looking at the image again: dialogue text at y~445 and prompt at ~590. The measurement says line at 468 and prompt at 512 in current state. The screenshot shows quote at 354, speaker at 405, line 445, prompt 590. Difference indicates `.line` had min-height applied (because :has selector was maybe not matching at screenshot time? It is supported). Actually if `.line{min-height:5.4em}` at 17px = 91.8px, then line box 468→560, prompt 512? Hmm choices y512 would overlap. No.

Maybe the screenshot was taken while `.panel:has(.choices:not(:empty)) .line{min-height:0}` didn't exist yet. It was likely from before that fix. Current state is good.

At small 360x640, docH=807 so requires scrolling, but choices fit within panel (panel y312 h479 ends 791; viewport 640). So user scrolls to see choices. That's acceptable-ish but our next-move item was to compact small phones. Could add a `@media (max-height:700px) and (max-width:900px)` rule to reduce portrait height and panel min-height so the panel fits viewport without scroll. At 360x640: HUD top 14 + ~42 => content starts 78. Portrait 220 + gap 14 = 312. Panel 479 => 791. To fit 640 need save 151px. Reduce portrait to 150, panel compress by ~80. Choices are 3×70 + gaps etc. Can compact choice padding/font on short phones. Let's design:

@media (max-height:700px) and (max-width:900px):
- .stage{padding-top:calc(70px + safe top); gap:10px; padding-bottom:8px}
- .portrait-card{height:clamp(150px,26dvh,190px); min-height:150px}
- .portrait{width:min(76%,330px)}
- .panel{min-height:0; padding:14px 14px 10px}
- .chapter-quote{display:none} (saves 35)
- .dialogue{padding:10px 0 6px; min-height:0} perhaps without choices dialogue min-height needs something; but panel will size to content, that's fine on short screens.
- .line{font-size:15.5px; line-height:1.65; min-height:3.2em} .line.narr{font-size:13.5px; min-height:3.6em}
- .choices{gap:7px}
