But is this necessary? The game is playable by scrolling, as the summary says. Yet compaction would improve. However there's risk of breaking nice layouts. We can add scoped media query for short phones. Also for 844x390 landscape already works.

Also title with name entry on small phone might be tight but tested.

Let me first check screenshots of small play and title from viewports run.

Small (360x640) is quite scroll-heavy: title fits, play screen cut off at bottom (continue button below fold), choices 3rd below fold. Scrolling works, but compaction would make it much better. Let's implement the compact media query for height<=700 width<=900. Need to be careful that at 390x844 nothing changes, tablet 768x1024 unaffected.

Also note small-title: portrait is large with empty space between portrait and title? It's at 640 height; title screen uses align-items flex-end, portrait fixed at top 14 height 26dvh=166 min 170. Looks fine but there's a gap because portrait height 170, title block bottom. Acceptable.

Let's add media query after max-width:420 block (before max-height:700 min-width:901). It must come after max-width:420 so overrides portrait height. Specificity: media both active at 360x640 (max-height:700 + max-width:900). Our rule later wins.

