But when choices aren't present, `.line` min-height 3.3em is good; the panel height shrinks to content and Continue at bottom. The panel no longer has min-height 420, so play screen fits in viewport. Grid stage min-height 100dvh and align-items start: portrait 160+ panel ~300 total 470 < 640, leaving empty bottom space. Hmm with align start it will all sit at top and empty bottom. That's okay but maybe visually top-heavy. Could center portrait/panel vertically? The stage min-height 100dvh, align-items:start. Could set for short: align-content:center? With stage grid and min-height 100dvh; align-items:start means items at top; there'd be 100px blank at bottom. Better than requiring scroll. But maybe make stage `align-content:center` and padding, so group centered. However panel content grows with choices. Use `align-content:center` for short screens. Yet grid has one column, two rows; align-content center will center both rows in container. That seems nice.

Let's test it. But note the hud is fixed overlay at top, so stage padding-top 68 leaves room.

